# KNOWN-GOOD stock boot log — RG35XX H V4.0 (captured by owner over UART)
# Date: 2026-11-16. Card: stock SD (untouched). Two consecutive boots shown;
# the second boot follows an ~86 s suspend window (hci errors) — whether the
# unit rebooted itself or was power-cycled there is UNCONFIRMED (see note).
# Verbatim capture; annotations at the end are ours (Lead), not device output.
#
# NOTE (suspend vs reboot): the first session shows `hci: ERR: hcd is null`
# at ~86 s followed by BOOT0 (cold boot). The hw agent separately observed a
# clean 7.1 s suspend/resume cycle. Both observations stand; suspend path
# needs one instrumented cycle (UART kept open, no input) to disambiguate.

